# SignerReach v0.1.1

SignerReach v0.1.1 is published from verified main commit
`{{SOURCE_COMMIT}}`.

## What changed since v0.1.0

- The checker accepts account snapshots recorded at Stellar **Protocol 29 or
  30**. Every other protocol version still gives `INCONCLUSIVE`
  (`SR-RULES-01`). v0.1.0 accepted Protocol 29 only.
- The development replay tool can test a named protocol with
  `--network-protocol 29` or `--network-protocol 30`. The default is 29.
- The documentation, the evidence index and the contributor guides describe the
  Protocol 30 evidence and the contribution process.

## Included

- `signerreach check` evaluates an account snapshot, ordered transaction plan
  and declared signer availability, returning deterministic text or JSON with
  `SAFE WITHIN SCOPE`, `UNSAFE` or `INCONCLUSIVE`.
- `signerreach fetch` performs a constrained, read-only Horizon account read
  and emits a provenance-bearing snapshot.
- The release includes bounded JSON parsing, stable diagnostics and reports,
  offline checking, fixture coverage and the documentation book.
- The `tools/replay` program remains a development-only Testnet harness and is
  not part of the shipped CLI or its release dependencies.

## Protocol 29 and 30 scope

This release supports the verified Stellar **Protocol 29 and Protocol 30** rules
for one classic G-address account, ed25519 signers and the implemented
`SetOptions` subset. It models transaction pre-state authorization, ordered
transactions, availability scenarios and the LOW envelope plus MEDIUM/HIGH
operation thresholds relevant to that subset.

The Protocol 30 evidence is a Testnet observation. The seven chain-backed
fixtures and the FX-01 follow-up produced the expected outcomes on a Testnet
running Protocol 30, and the stellar-core 29.0.0 and 30.0.0 source files for
signature checking and `SetOptions` are identical. It does not cover inputs
outside those cases.

Contract and muxed accounts, fee-bump transactions, unsupported signer types,
other operation types, additional source accounts, sponsorship, account flags
and reserve effects remain outside the safe-verdict boundary and are reported or
documented as `INCONCLUSIVE` where applicable.

## Security boundaries and limitations

The shipped CLI never accepts, stores or uses private signing keys, never signs
transactions and never submits them. `check` is offline. `fetch` uses
constrained read-only Horizon requests. The replay harness creates temporary
Testnet keys only for explicitly run development experiments and is not a
production transaction path. The evidence records below come from that harness.

This project has not received an independent security audit. Results aid human
review and do not guarantee key custody, current state, reserve sufficiency or
successful future submission. Crates.io publication remains disabled
(`publish = false`).

## Reproducible evidence

- [2026-10-13 Testnet observations](https://github.com/signerreach/signerreach/blob/main/docs/evidence/testnet-2026-10-13/README.md) (Protocol 29)
- [2026-10-19 seven-fixture replay](https://github.com/signerreach/signerreach/blob/main/docs/evidence/replay-2026-10-19/README.md) (Protocol 29)
- [2026-11-01 FX-01 follow-up replay](https://github.com/signerreach/signerreach/blob/main/docs/evidence/replay-2026-11-01-fx-01-followup/README.md) (Protocol 29)
- [2026-11-04 Protocol 30 replay](https://github.com/signerreach/signerreach/blob/main/docs/evidence/replay-2026-11-04-protocol-30/README.md) (Protocol 30)

The FX-01 follow-up repeated the master-only rejection after raising HIGH to 2,
at Protocol 29 and again at Protocol 30. The records do not verify every
historical follow-up case, current account state or behavior beyond the recorded
evidence.

